<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Barda</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Partav, Bardha'a, Barda'a</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Barda is a town in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> near the Kura river, the ancient Partav, which replaced Kabala as the capital of Caucasian Albania in the 5th century. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a>, as Bardha'a, it was one of the largest cities of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> and the seat of governors of Arran. It was sacked by the Rus' in 943–944 and later declined.</p></div>
